1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A motorcycle trip can produce hundreds of gigabytes of footage.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The memorable story is buried across GPS timestamps and long video files.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Ride Storyteller uses an evidence-seeking agent to find moments worth reviewing.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The system parses the route locally and extracts explainable GPS events.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,000
These include departure, stops, elevation and direction changes, and arrival.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
GPS proposes where to look. It never claims what the camera saw.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:03,000
For a high-interest event, the Story Agent requests video evidence.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:16,000
It searches for matching media and analyzes only the requested interval.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Missing media or invalid analysis fails safely to human review.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:36,000
A GPS match is not enough. Every candidate starts as awaiting evidence.

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Evidence can be confirmed or rejected with an attributed source.

12
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Only confirmed candidates can enter the render plan.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:02,000
The same private-data boundary runs as a synthetic-only Google ADK agent in Tokyo.

14
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:15,000
It sends a fixed synthetic event and returns no model text or private data.

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
IBM Bob reviewed the architecture and identified priority implementation gaps.

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
We implemented those findings and retained before-and-after test evidence.

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:45,000
REAL MEDIA GATE: final footage evidence is not available in this draft.

18
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Replace this cue only after approved clip analysis and human evidence review.

19
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Ride Storyteller turns telemetry into questions, video into evidence, and evidence into story.
